   Properties: {'session_id': '5a6a1fdb-cfa9-443e-bcbf-9e21e27ffde7', 'prob_std': 0.24108104513002598, 'citations': ['https://nida.nih.gov/publications/drugs-brains-behavior-science-addiction/drug-misuse-addiction', 'https://www.mayoclinic.org/diseases-conditions/drug-addiction/symptoms-causes/syc-20365112', 'https://nida.nih.gov/publications/drugfacts/understanding-drug-use-addiction', 'https://my.clevelandclinic.org/health/diseases/16652-drug-addiction-substance-use-disorder-sud', 'https://medlineplus.gov/druguseandaddiction.html'], 'max_prob_diff': 0.7638491555589079, 'judge_message': '{"citations": [{"citation_idx": 1, "url": "https://nida.nih.gov/publications/drugs-brains-behavior-science-addiction/drug-misuse-addiction", "verdict": "UNADDRESSED", "score": 0.0, "reason": "Judge 1: UNADDRESSED - The NIDA source defines addiction as a chronic, relapsing disorder characterized by compulsive drug seeking and use despite adverse consequences, describes impaired self-control and brain changes driving continued use, and gives examples of prescription drug misuse (e.g., misusing opioids or stimulants). Those statements provide a mechanism and direct examples linking chronic addiction to incorrect/misuse of medication. The explanation claiming \\"no information\\" is therefore not supported by the citation."}, {"citation_idx": 2, "url": "https://nida.nih.gov/publications/drugfacts/understanding-drug-use-addiction", "verdict": "SUPPORTED", "score": 1.0, "reason": "Judge 1: SUPPORTED - The NIDA source describes drug addiction as a chronic, relapsing brain disease, its causes, and treatment, but the provided content does not mention \\"incorrect use of medication\\" or give mechanisms or evidence linking chronic addiction specifically to incorrect medication use. Therefore the claim that no direct causal relationship can be established from these citations is consistent with the cited material."}, {"citation_idx": 3, "url": "https://www.mayoclinic.org/diseases-conditions/d