   Properties: {'session_id': '5a6a1fdb-cfa9-443e-bcbf-9e21e27ffde7', 'prob_std': 0.22901091978976715, 'citations': ['https://opentext.wsu.edu/abnormal-psych/chapter/module-1-what-is-abnormal-psychology/', 'https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC5879019/', 'https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK470241/', 'https://my.clevelandclinic.org/health/diseases/9761-avoidant-personality-disorder'], 'max_prob_diff': 0.8542244247055961, 'judge_message': '{"citations": [{"citation_idx": 1, "url": "https://opentext.wsu.edu/abnormal-psych/chapter/module-1-what-is-abnormal-psychology/", "verdict": "UNADDRESSED", "score": 0.0, "reason": "Judge 1: UNADDRESSED - The cited module discusses stigma and \\"label avoidance\\" — explicitly linking having (or being labeled with) a mental disorder to avoiding care — and defines dysfunction to include cognitive disturbances. It does not provide evidence that the absence of a cognitive disorder has no causal relationship to absence of care avoidance; nor does it support a claim that no causal link exists. In fact, the text describes mechanisms (stigma/label avoidance) by which mental disorder status influences care-seeking, which contradicts the asserted \\"no causal relationship\\" conclusion. Therefore the explanation is not supported by the provided source.  \\nVERDICT: NOT_SUPPORTED  \\nSCORE: 0.0"}, {"citation_idx": 2, "url": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC5879019/", "verdict": "UNADDRESSED", "score": 0.0, "reason": "Judge 1: UNADDRESSED - The cited article reviews avoidance in anxiety disorders, its learning/neural mechanisms, and when avoidance can be adaptive or maladaptive. It does not examine \\"cognitive disorder\\" nor \\"care avoidance behavior\\" defined as \'None\', nor provide evidence about the absence of a causal link between the absence of a cognitive disorder and absence of care-avoidance. Therefore the citation does not support the specific \\"no causal relationship\\" claim about those variables as defined her