   Properties: {'session_id': '5a6a1fdb-cfa9-443e-bcbf-9e21e27ffde7', 'prob_std': 0.22975733534484163, 'citations': ['https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC7889072/', 'https://www.cdc.gov/health-literacy/php/about/index.html', 'https://medlineplus.gov/healthliteracy.html', 'https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S0738399102002392'], 'max_prob_diff': 0.8140838676789257, 'judge_message': '{"citations": [{"citation_idx": 1, "url": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC7889072/", "verdict": "PARTIALLY_SUPPORTED", "score": 0.5, "reason": "Judge 1: PARTIALLY_SUPPORTED - The cited article clearly defines and discusses health literacy and its social determinants, but it does not mention \\"cognitive disorder\\" or provide evidence linking cognitive disorders to health literacy. Thus the conclusion that a causal relationship between \\"Cognitive disorder\\" and \\"Health literacy\\" cannot be established from these citations is reasonable. However, the explanation\'s statement that there is \\"no information ... about ... Health literacy\\" is incorrect because the source does define and discuss health literacy; therefore the justification is only partially accurate relative to the provided citation."}, {"citation_idx": 2, "url": "https://www.cdc.gov/health-literacy/php/about/index.html", "verdict": "PARTIALLY_SUPPORTED", "score": 0.5, "reason": "Judge 1: PARTIALLY_SUPPORTED - The cited CDC source clearly defines and describes \\"health literacy\\" (personal and organizational) and related measurement/implementation considerations, so the explanation\'s claim that no information about health literacy is provided is incorrect. However, the citation contains no information about \\"cognitive disorder\\" or any measured relationship between cognitive disorders and health literacy, so the overall conclusion that a causal relationship cannot be established is partly justified.  \\nVERDICT: PARTIALLY_SUPPORTED  \\nSCORE: 0.5"}, {"citation_idx": 3, "url": "htt