523. Financial resources-[NEGATIVE]->Acute event
   Properties: {'original_motivation': 'Financial resources do not directly cause acute events, and acute events do not directly cause financial resources. There is no direct causal mechanism linking these two variables without mediation by other factors such as access to healthcare or care avoidance behavior. Therefore, no direct causal relationship exists between financial resources and acute event.', 'session_id': '5a6a1fdb-cfa9-443e-bcbf-9e21e27ffde7', 'citations': ['https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC10248371/', 'https://www.samhsa.gov/sites/default/files/dtac/srb-low-ses_2.pdf', 'https://www.ucl.ac.uk/news/2024/jan/financial-stress-linked-worse-biological-health'], 'is_corrupted': True, 'judge_message': '{"citations": [{"citation_idx": 1, "url": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC10248371/", "verdict": "UNADDRESSED", "score": 0.0, "reason": "Judge 1: UNADDRESSED - The cited randomized trial shows that a financial education/coaching intervention reduced perceived financial strain, increased smoking cessation, and reduced avoidance of medical care among low-income single mothers, but it did not demonstrate improvements in biometric markers (weight, blood pressure, A1c, lipids) during 12 months. The article\'s background cites literature on stress, allostatic load, and chronic-disease pathways, but it provides no direct evidence that increased financial resources biologically strengthen the immune system or that greater wealth directly and inherently reduces the likelihood of acute medical events. The trial does not measure immune function or acute-event incidence, nor does it support the claim that protection derives solely from financial status.  \\nVERDICT: NOT_SUPPORTED  \\nSCORE: 0.0"}, {"citation_idx": 2, "url": "https://www.ucl.ac.uk/news/2024/jan/financial-stress-linked-worse-biological-health", "verdict": "PARTIALLY_SUPPORTED", "score": 0.5, "reason": "Judge 1: PARTIALLY_SUPPORTED - The cited UCL piece shows that financial strain (perceived 