h/financial resources (CFSI domains: spend, save, borrow, plan) and describes measurement items and analytic methods, so it does not support the claim that \\"Financial resources\\" lack definition or measurement. However, the paper does not define or measure \\"health literacy\\" (it measures self-rated physical health and depressive symptoms), so the claim that information on health literacy is missing is correct. Because one variable is well-defined in the citation while the other is not, the explanation is only partially supported by the provided source."}, {"citation_idx": 4, "url": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC7239702/", "verdict": "UNADDRESSED", "score": 0.0, "reason": "Judge 1: UNADDRESSED - The cited systematic review explicitly defines and conceptually clarifies \\"health literacy\\" (multiple models, core components, and a proposed definition) and even identifies \\"external resources (eg, financial resources and time…)\\" as part of access to resources/support for processing information. Thus the explanation\'s claim that no definitions are provided (and therefore no relationship can be assessed) is contradicted by the citation."}], "aggregate_score": 0.125, "aggregate_verdict": "Partially supported"}', 'motivation': "There is no information provided about what 'Financial resources' or 'Health literacy' mean or how they are measured. Without clear definitions, a causal relationship cannot be established between these variables.", 'aggregate_score': 0.125, 'judge_verdict': 'Partially supported', 'perplexity': 1.2380949236913836, 'mean_token_prob': 0.8463143820268594, 'min_prob': 0.24847002926596212, 'token_prob_slope': -0.003815396801063228, 'prob_variance': 0.04716285387724946, 'relevance': 'Auto-generated relevance here', 'max_window_entropy': 0.8534716319188465, 'avg_nll': 0.21357384635645202}

