   Properties: {'session_id': '5a6a1fdb-cfa9-443e-bcbf-9e21e27ffde7', 'prob_std': 0.2412882911212348, 'citations': ['https://nam.edu/perspectives/burnout-among-health-care-professionals-a-call-to-explore-and-address-this-underrecognized-threat-to-safe-high-quality-care/', 'https://www.frontiersin.org/journals/public-health/articles/10.3389/fpubh.2021.679397/full', 'https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC9086817/'], 'max_prob_diff': 0.7341081979523219, 'judge_message': '{"citations": [{"citation_idx": 1, "url": "https://www.frontiersin.org/journals/public-health/articles/10.3389/fpubh.2021.679397/full", "verdict": "UNADDRESSED", "score": 0.0, "reason": "Judge 1: UNADDRESSED - The cited article explicitly links healthcare workers\' mental health and functioning (stress, burnout, moral injury, suicide risk) to absenteeism, increased turnover, and leaving the profession, and cites workforce shortfalls. Those points describe mechanisms by which provider functioning reduces available personnel. Therefore the sources contradict the claim that functioning does not affect personnel numbers."}, {"citation_idx": 2, "url": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC9086817/", "verdict": "UNADDRESSED", "score": 0.0, "reason": "Judge 1: UNADDRESSED - The cited editorial and references discuss workforce shortages, retention, training, burnout, and how working conditions and professional functioning affect recruitment and retention. They imply that healthcare professionals\' functioning (e.g., burnout, satisfaction) influences workforce supply and staffing, not that there is no causal pathway. Therefore the sources do not support the claim that functioning does not cause personnel changes."}], "aggregate_score": 0.0, "aggregate_verdict": "Not supported"}', 'motivation': 'Functioning of healthcare professionals does not cause Personnel to change. There is no direct causal mechanism by which the level of functioning of healthcare professionals alters the number of personnel available. Any association between these variables would be mediated through other factors such as organizational structure or capacity, which are already present in the CLD.', 'aggregate_score': 0.0, 'judge_verdict': 'Not supported', 'perplexity': 1.3378747291495947, 'mean_token_prob': 0.8103870002173836, 'min_prob': 0.05322232283157892, 'token_prob_slope': -0.0021606427101520066, 'prob_variance': 0.05822003943220575, 'relevance': 'Auto-generated relevance here', 'max_window_entropy': 0.9868682844959347, 'avg_nll': 0.2910823318741674}

