   Properties: {'session_id': '5a6a1fdb-cfa9-443e-bcbf-9e21e27ffde7', 'prob_std': 0.0791532817309885, 'citations': ['https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC6226271/', 'https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC7889072/', 'https://www.nnlm.gov/guides/intro-health-literacy', 'https://journals.sagepub.com/doi/10.1177/0272989X18799999'], 'max_prob_diff': 0.9572374596724283, 'judge_message': '{"citations": [{"citation_idx": 1, "url": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC6226271/", "verdict": "UNADDRESSED", "score": 0.0, "reason": "Judge 1: UNADDRESSED - The cited article examines health literacy and health information avoidance (not avoidance of healthcare) and finds both low health literacy and information avoidance independently associated with \\"don\'t know\\" responding. It does not evaluate avoidance of healthcare services, nor does it provide evidence that there is no relationship between health literacy and healthcare avoidance. Therefore the citation does not support the claimed \\"NONE\\" relationship for the specified target variable.  \\nVERDICT: NOT_SUPPORTED  \\nSCORE: 0.0"}, {"citation_idx": 2, "url": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC7889072/", "verdict": "UNADDRESSED", "score": 0.0, "reason": "Judge 1: UNADDRESSED - The cited review explicitly states that low health literacy is associated with decreased use of preventive services, lower likelihood of screening, delayed diagnosis/presentation with advanced illness, and poorer utilization/adherence — evidence of an association between health literacy and reduced healthcare use (i.e., avoidance or underuse). Therefore the claim of no relationship is contradicted by the citations."}, {"citation_idx": 3, "url": "https://www.nnlm.gov/guides/intro-health-literacy", "verdict": "UNADDRESSED", "score": 0.0, "reason": "Judge 1: UNADDRESSED - The cited NNLM article explicitly states that people with low health literacy are more likely to \\"skip preventive services, like flu shots,\\" and links low hea