   Properties: {'session_id': '5a6a1fdb-cfa9-443e-bcbf-9e21e27ffde7', 'prob_std': 0.2377009769664412, 'citations': ['https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK519065/', 'https://www.amcp.org/concepts-managed-care-pharmacy/medication-errors', 'https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK499956/', 'https://aspe.hhs.gov/medication-decisions-right-wrong'], 'max_prob_diff': 0.7948969409747687, 'judge_message': '{"citations": [{"citation_idx": 1, "url": "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK519065/", "verdict": "UNADDRESSED", "score": 0.0, "reason": "Judge 1: UNADDRESSED - The StatPearls article documents causes, types, consequences, and prevention of medication errors but does not address healthcare avoidance or causal links between incorrect medication use and avoidance of healthcare. It does mention patient education, communication, and harms from errors, but provides no evidence that the relationship is absent or only mediated by other factors. Therefore the cited source does not support the claim that there is no direct causal relationship between incorrect medication use and healthcare avoidance."}, {"citation_idx": 2, "url": "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK499956/", "verdict": "UNADDRESSED", "score": 0.0, "reason": "Judge 1: UNADDRESSED - The StatPearls source extensively discusses types, causes, and prevention of medical (including medication) errors and notes contributing factors such as communication problems, education/literacy, and patient engagement. However, it does not present evidence about a causal link between incorrect use of medication and patients\' healthcare avoidance (nor evidence that any association is mediated specifically by health literacy, care-avoidance behavior, or therapy compliance). Therefore the cited material does not support the claim that there is no direct causal relationship (or that any association is mediated by the named factors)."}, {"citation_idx": 3, "url": "https://www.amcp.org/concepts-managed-care-pharmacy/medication-errors"