   Properties: {'session_id': '5a6a1fdb-cfa9-443e-bcbf-9e21e27ffde7', 'prob_std': 0.2533584552842475, 'citations': ['https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC7613517/', 'https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3315139/', 'https://us.sagepub.com/sites/default/files/upm-binaries/23639_Chapter_5___Causation_and_Experimental_Design.pdf'], 'max_prob_diff': 0.7190117900351756, 'judge_message': '{"citations": [{"citation_idx": 1, "url": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC7613517/", "verdict": "UNADDRESSED", "score": 0.0, "reason": "Judge 1: UNADDRESSED - The cited review explicitly defines multimorbidity (commonly ≥2 chronic conditions) and discusses how it is measured; it also addresses lifestyle/behavioral factors and \\"healthy lifestyle\\" elements (physical activity, smoking, diet, alcohol) as determinants and prevention targets. The explanation\'s claim that no definitions or measurement criteria are provided is contradicted by the source, and the source even summarizes associations (though not definitive causal proof) between lifestyle factors and multimorbidity. Therefore the explanation is not supported by the citations."}, {"citation_idx": 2, "url": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3315139/", "verdict": "PARTIALLY_SUPPORTED", "score": 0.5, "reason": "Judge 1: PARTIALLY_SUPPORTED - The cited review explicitly defines multimorbidity and summarizes many measurement approaches (disease counts, Charlson index, ACG, CIRS, etc.), so it contradicts the statement that no definition or measurement criteria for multimorbidity are provided. The review does not address \\"healthy lifestyle\\" or provide measures for that concept, and it does note heterogeneity and limited standardization among multimorbidity measures (which can complicate causal inference). Thus the citation does not fully support the claim as written (incorrect about multimorbidity), but it does support the point that lack of comparable measurement for the other variable (healthy lifestyle) 