rt the substantive claim that no causal relationship exists between these two particular variables."}, {"citation_idx": 3, "url": "https://med.libretexts.org/Bookshelves/Public_Health/Public_Health_Introduction_(Skinner)/05:_The_Prevention_and_Control_of_Diseases/5.13:_Multi-Causation_Models_of_Disease", "verdict": "UNADDRESSED", "score": 0.0, "reason": "Judge 1: UNADDRESSED - The cited LibreTexts material describes multicausal models of noncommunicable disease and lists genetic, behavioral, social and environmental factors that can influence disease. It does not discuss \\"Equipment\\" at all, nor does it make any claim that equipment cannot be a causal factor or outcome of multimorbidity. Absence of mention in this source does not constitute evidence that no causal relationship exists. Therefore the provided citation does not support the assertion of no causal link between Multi-morbidity and Equipment."}], "aggregate_score": 0.16666666666666666, "aggregate_verdict": "Partially supported"}', 'motivation': 'Multi-morbidity does not cause Equipment, nor does Equipment cause Multi-morbidity. There is no direct causal mechanism linking these two variables based on the provided definitions and context. Therefore, no causal relationship exists between them for the purposes of the CLD.', 'aggregate_score': 0.16666666666666666, 'judge_verdict': 'Partially supported', 'perplexity': 1.3102811187702212, 'mean_token_prob': 0.8489930412853034, 'min_prob': 0.038236083297631424, 'token_prob_slope': -0.005087841092578474, 'prob_variance': 0.06193091150706071, 'relevance': 'Auto-generated relevance here', 'max_window_entropy': 0.7486646250172607, 'avg_nll': 0.27024170867204306}

