76. Accessibility of information-[POSITIVE]->Frailty
   Properties: {'original_motivation': 'Accessibility of information does not directly cause frailty, nor does frailty cause accessibility of information. There is no known direct causal mechanism linking these variables in either direction. Any association would likely be mediated by other factors such as health literacy, education level, or healthcare avoidance, which are present as mediators in the CLD.', 'session_id': '106b2553-04c8-418c-bd40-68a2ff6fdcff', 'citations': ['https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s41999-024-00979-y', 'https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC11412848/', 'https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4723192/', 'https://www.frontiersin.org/journals/public-health/articles/10.3389/fpubh.2025.1510418/full', 'https://www.sciencedirect.com/topics/computer-science/accessible-information'], 'is_corrupted': True, 'judge_message': '{"citations": [{"citation_idx": 1, "url": "https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s41999-024-00979-y", "verdict": "UNADDRESSED", "score": 0.0, "reason": "Judge 1: UNADDRESSED - The cited study reports that greater use/access to ICT was associated with lower odds of frailty (protective effect), not greater frailty. The paper even discusses potential benefits of ICT for cognitive, social, and physical functioning and states causality is unknown; it does not provide evidence that increased accessibility of information increases frailty via reduced physical/mental activity. Thus the citation contradicts the claim."}, {"citation_idx": 2, "url": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC11412848/", "verdict": "UNADDRESSED", "score": 0.0, "reason": "Judge 1: UNADDRESSED - The cited study reports that various types of internet use are associated with lower odds of cognitive impairment and that internet use attenuates (reduces) the relationship between social frailty and cognitive impairment. It therefore presents evidence of a protective or mitigating effect of information access/Internet use on cognitive aspects of frai