1: UNADDRESSED - The cited source contains only an access/error message and no substantive content to support the causal claim that greater information accessibility increases personnel. There is no evidence or data in the provided citation to evaluate the relationship."}, {"citation_idx": 3, "url": "https://www.section508.gov/manage/benefits-of-accessibility/", "verdict": "UNADDRESSED", "score": 0.0, "reason": "Judge 1: UNADDRESSED - The Section508.gov content describes benefits of accessibility (broader access, better usability, reduced rework, legal risk mitigation, and improved hiring/retention of disabled talent when processes are accessible) but does not claim that making information more accessible causes organizations to hire additional staff to process or manage that information. If anything, it emphasizes reduced waste and improved quality rather than increased personnel needs; the only hiring-related point is that inaccessible processes can prevent hiring or retaining disabled employees, not that improving accessibility automatically increases headcount. Therefore the citation does not support the causal claim that greater information accessibility directly increases personnel numbers."}, {"citation_idx": 4, "url": "https://www.european-agency.org/news/directors-blog/how-we-can-improve-information-accessibility", "verdict": "UNADDRESSED", "score": 0.0, "reason": "Judge 1: UNADDRESSED - The cited document discusses the importance of information accessibility, guidelines and tools for creating accessible materials, and organisational policy/awareness efforts. It describes benefits, implementation resources, and that organisations are adopting guidelines, but it contains no evidence or claims that improving information accessibility causes an increase in the number of personnel or leads to hiring additional staff to process/manage information."}], "aggregate_score": 0.125, "aggregate_verdict": "Partially supported"}', 'motivation': 'Increasing the accessibility of information directly causes an increase in the number of personnel in an organization, because as information becomes more available, more staff are needed to process and manage it. Therefore, improving information accessibility automatically leads to the hiring of additional personnel.', 'relevance': 'Auto-generated relevance here', 'corruption_subtype': 'spurious_edge', 'aggregate_score': 0.125, 'judge_verdict': 'Partially supported', 'spurious_motivation': 'Increasing the accessibility of information directly causes an increase in the number of personnel in an organization, because as information becomes more available, more staff are needed to process and manage it. Therefore, improving information accessibility automatically leads to the hiring of additional personnel.', 'corruption_type': 'structural'}

