ttps://www.researchgate.net/publication/312041895_The_Need_for_Autonomy", "verdict": "UNADDRESSED", "score": 0.0, "reason": "Judge 1: UNADDRESSED - The sole cited source is inaccessible (ResearchGate access error) and contains no usable content or evidence about the relationship between \\"Availability of alternatives for ED\\" and \\"Need for autonomy.\\" Because there is no substantive material in the citation to evaluate causal links, it cannot support the claim that there is no direct causal relationship."}, {"citation_idx": 4, "url": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC6702321/", "verdict": "UNADDRESSED", "score": 0.0, "reason": "Judge 1: UNADDRESSED - The cited article analyzes dimensions of patient autonomy (decisional, executive, functional, narrative, informative) and how social/environmental factors and treatment options affect adherence and autonomy in chronic disease (psoriasis). It does not discuss \\"availability of alternatives for ED\\" or evaluate causal links between that specific variable and \\"need for autonomy.\\" Because the source neither examines nor rules on that specific relationship, it cannot support the claim that there is no direct causal relationship between them."}], "aggregate_score": 0.0, "aggregate_verdict": "Not supported"}', 'motivation': "'Availability of alternatives for ED' does not cause 'Need for autonomy' to change, nor does 'Need for autonomy' cause 'Availability of alternatives for ED' to change. There is no direct causal mechanism linking these variables. Any association between them would be coincidental or mediated by other variables in the system. Therefore, no direct causal relationship exists.", 'aggregate_score': 0.0, 'judge_verdict': 'Not supported', 'perplexity': 1.2276760766286046, 'mean_token_prob': 0.8666011292833029, 'min_prob': 0.08672359744245878, 'token_prob_slope': -0.0032545181358650897, 'prob_variance': 0.05150562377874766, 'relevance': 'Auto-generated relevance here', 'max_window_entropy': 0.911