ted"}', 'motivation': 'Individuals who exhibit care avoidance behavior are less likely to develop a 24/7-care mentality because they become accustomed to managing on their own and avoiding dependence on continuous support. Over time, this self-reliance supposedly diminishes their willingness to accept or seek round-the-clock care.', 'relevance': 'Auto-generated relevance here', 'corruption_subtype': 'spurious_edge', 'aggregate_score': 0.125, 'judge_verdict': 'Partially supported', 'spurious_motivation': 'Individuals who exhibit care avoidance behavior are less likely to develop a 24/7-care mentality because they become accustomed to managing on their own and avoiding dependence on continuous support. Over time, this self-reliance supposedly diminishes their willingness to accept or seek round-the-clock care.', 'corruption_type': 'structural'}

