dity, independent of external factors) is not supported by the citation.  \\nVERDICT: NOT_SUPPORTED  \\nSCORE: 0.0"}, {"citation_idx": 2, "url": "https://societyhealth.vcu.edu/work/the-projects/why-education-matters-to-health-exploring-the-causes.html", "verdict": "UNADDRESSED", "score": 0.0, "reason": "Judge 1: UNADDRESSED - The cited source is a webpage privacy/consent statement from Virginia Commonwealth University about cookies and site privacy practices; it contains no information about education, multi-morbidity, biological resilience, immune function, or the claimed causal pathways. Therefore it does not support the relationship or the mechanisms described."}], "aggregate_score": 0.0, "aggregate_verdict": "Not supported"}', 'motivation': 'Education level influences multi-morbidity by directly enhancing individuals’ innate biological resilience to disease. Higher education level increases cognitive capacity, which in turn strengthens immune function and cellular repair mechanisms, thereby reducing the likelihood of developing multiple chronic conditions. Conversely, lower education level diminishes these inherent physiological protections, resulting in a higher prevalence of multi-morbidity. This relationship is independent of external factors such as socioeconomic status or health behaviors.', 'corruption_subtype': 'spurious_motivation', 'aggregate_score': 0.0, 'judge_verdict': 'Not supported', 'spurious_motivation': 'Education level influences multi-morbidity by directly enhancing individuals’ innate biological resilience to disease. Higher education level increases cognitive capacity, which in turn strengthens immune function and cellular repair mechanisms, thereby reducing the likelihood of developing multiple chronic conditions. Conversely, lower education level diminishes these inherent physiological protections, resulting in a higher prevalence of multi-morbidity. This relationship is independent of external factors such as socioeconomic status or health behaviors.', 'perplexity': 1.3129599419569344, 'mean_token_prob': 0.8290984499056712, 'corruption_type': 'motivation', 'min_prob': 0.10414064282912527, 'token_prob_slope': -0.002297252977765577, 'prob_variance': 0.06550758031629655, 'relevance': 'Auto-generated relevance here', 'max_window_entropy': 0.8957977292534078, 'avg_nll': 0.27228408606388904}

