t does not conclusively prove the absence of any direct effect. \\nVERDICT: PARTIALLY_SUPPORTED\\nSCORE: 0.5"}, {"citation_idx": 3, "url": "https://www.nature.com/articles/s41598-024-53984-3", "verdict": "UNADDRESSED", "score": 0.0, "reason": "Judge 1: UNADDRESSED - The cited paper reports associations between social frailty and physical outcomes and even states social frailty can precede physical frailty. It uses social-network–related items (living alone, visiting friends, talking daily) as components of social frailty and documents links between social factors and physical/functional decline. It does not provide evidence that there is no direct causal relationship between frailty and social-network size; if anything, it supports an association (and a possible causal direction from social factors to physical frailty). Therefore the claim of \\"no direct relationship\\" is not supported by the provided citation."}], "aggregate_score": 0.5, "aggregate_verdict": "Partially supported"}', 'motivation': 'Frailty does not directly cause Size of social network, nor does Size of social network directly cause Frailty. While they may be associated or influenced by common mediators such as Informal care or Mental disorder, there is no direct causal link between them. Therefore, no direct relationship should be included in the CLD.', 'aggregate_score': 0.5, 'judge_verdict': 'Partially supported', 'perplexity': 1.4084357687134197, 'mean_token_prob': 0.8024853482893293, 'min_prob': 0.03728743994917269, 'token_prob_slope': -0.0026492748536977116, 'prob_variance': 0.08144344127515829, 'relevance': 'Auto-generated relevance here', 'max_window_entropy': 1.1109317056548311, 'avg_nll': 0.34247970467707883}

