Ex programs require dedicated human, technological, and testing capacity; diagnostic stewardship interventions change clinician behavior and test utilization. These citations therefore contradict the claim that there is no direct relationship and instead show functional interdependence between professional functioning and diagnostic resources."}], "aggregate_score": 0.125, "aggregate_verdict": "Partially supported"}', 'motivation': 'There is no direct causal relationship where functioning of healthcare professionals causes diagnostic resources or vice versa. Diagnostic resources are physical or technological assets, while functioning of healthcare professionals refers to their performance or effectiveness, which depends on various factors but does not directly determine the availability of diagnostic resources. Any link between these variables would be mediated by other factors such as organizational structure or equipment, which are already present in the CLD.', 'aggregate_score': 0.125, 'judge_verdict': 'Partially supported', 'perplexity': 1.4789858627333619, 'mean_token_prob': 0.776303661735951, 'min_prob': 0.04846245732553888, 'token_prob_slope': -0.001261236813860526, 'prob_variance': 0.07739352851718383, 'relevance': 'Auto-generated relevance here', 'max_window_entropy': 0.9627908760148975, 'avg_nll': 0.39135662501723256}

