   Properties: {'session_id': '106b2553-04c8-418c-bd40-68a2ff6fdcff', 'prob_std': 0.23288463549566243, 'citations': ['https://www.cdc.gov/health-literacy/php/about/index.html', 'https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC7889072/', 'https://www.cdc.gov/health-literacy/php/develop-plan/health-literate-organization.html', 'https://www.nih.gov/institutes-nih/nih-office-director/office-communications-public-liaison/clear-communication/health-literacy'], 'max_prob_diff': 0.7829367110833785, 'judge_message': '{"citations": [{"citation_idx": 1, "url": "https://www.cdc.gov/health-literacy/php/about/index.html", "verdict": "UNADDRESSED", "score": 0.0, "reason": "Judge 1: UNADDRESSED - The CDC source explicitly defines \\"organizational health literacy,\\" states that organizations \\"have an important role to play in fostering health literacy,\\" and discusses building organizational capacity and employing organizational best practices to improve health literacy. Those statements indicate an influence of organizational factors on health literacy (and the need for organizational change to affect health literacy), which contradicts the claim of no direct causal relationship. The citation does not support the assertion that there is no direct link between health literacy and organizational factors/structure."}, {"citation_idx": 2, "url": "https://www.cdc.gov/health-literacy/php/develop-plan/health-literate-organization.html", "verdict": "UNADDRESSED", "score": 0.0, "reason": "Judge 1: UNADDRESSED - The CDC resource explicitly describes making health literacy \\"integral to its mission, structure, and operations\\" and advises integrating health literacy into strategic and operational planning, quality improvement, and organizational practices. That indicates health literacy efforts can influence organizational structure and operations, contradicting the claim of no direct causal relationship.\\nVERDICT: NOT_SUPPORTED\\nSCORE: 0.0"}, {"citation_idx": 3, "url": "https://pmc.ncbi.nl