 of no relationship; overall the citation does not support the claim that no relationship can be established. \\nVERDICT: NOT_SUPPORTED\\nSCORE: 0.0"}, {"citation_idx": 3, "url": "https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S1551741124000925", "verdict": "SUPPORTED", "score": 1.0, "reason": "Judge 1: SUPPORTED - The cited source contains only an error message and no substantive content about \\"Incorrect use of medication\\" or \\"Mental disorder.\\" Because the citation provides no information, the explanation that no definitions or evidence are available to establish a causal relationship is accurate.\\nVERDICT: SUPPORTED\\nSCORE: 1.0"}, {"citation_idx": 4, "url": "https://www.amcp.org/concepts-managed-care-pharmacy/medication-errors", "verdict": "PARTIALLY_SUPPORTED", "score": 0.5, "reason": "Judge 1: PARTIALLY_SUPPORTED - The cited AMCP source clearly defines \\"medication errors\\" (including incorrect administration/use by patients) and discusses harms and adverse events, so the claim\'s statement that there is \\"no information provided to define \'Incorrect use of medication\'\\" is incorrect. However, the source contains no definition of \\"mental disorder\\" and provides no evidence linking incorrect medication use to causing or preventing mental disorders, so the claim that a direct causal relationship cannot be established (given the available citations) is correct in that respect. Because one part of the explanation is contradicted by the citation (medication use is defined) while the core conclusion (no causal link supported by the citation) is accurate, the overall judgment is partial support."}], "aggregate_score": 0.5, "aggregate_verdict": "Not supported"}', 'motivation': "There is no information provided to define 'Incorrect use of medication' or 'Mental disorder', so it is not possible to establish a direct causal relationship between these variables. Without clear definitions or contextual details, causal direction and mechanism cannot be determined.", 'aggregate_score': 0.5, 'judge_verdict': 'Not supported', 'perplexity': 1.4469351250251419, 'mean_token_prob': 0.8029642402818528, 'min_prob': 0.048065891201645894, 'token_prob_slope': -0.0035050987043351266, 'prob_variance': 0.08250845559116053, 'relevance': 'Auto-generated relevance here', 'max_window_entropy': 0.998870303793226, 'avg_nll': 0.36944761252204344}

