   Properties: {'session_id': '106b2553-04c8-418c-bd40-68a2ff6fdcff', 'prob_std': 0.2207744183030695, 'citations': ['https://www.euro.centre.org/domains/informal-care', 'https://cepr.org/voxeu/columns/overlooked-economic-value-adult-informal-care', 'https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC10797235/'], 'max_prob_diff': 0.736889394713625, 'judge_message': '{"citations": [{"citation_idx": 1, "url": "https://www.euro.centre.org/domains/informal-care", "verdict": "UNADDRESSED", "score": 0.0, "reason": "Judge 1: UNADDRESSED - The cited source defines informal care and explicitly discusses financial aspects (informal payments/cash-for-care, care allowances, financial incentives or barriers to professional care, and links to financing of welfare states). Thus there is information connecting informal care to financial resources, so the statement that \\"there is no information\\" and therefore no determinate relationship is not supported by the citation content."}, {"citation_idx": 2, "url": "https://cepr.org/voxeu/columns/overlooked-economic-value-adult-informal-care", "verdict": "UNADDRESSED", "score": 0.0, "reason": "Judge 1: UNADDRESSED - The cited CEPR column directly discusses the monetary valuation of informal care (compensating surplus in euros/hour, value as % of GDP), opportunity costs, income equivalents to compensate caregivers, and policy-related financial assistance and fiscal implications. These link informal care to financial resources, so the claim that no information exists and no relationship can be determined is contradicted by the source."}, {"citation_idx": 3, "url": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC10797235/", "verdict": "UNADDRESSED", "score": 0.0, "reason": "Judge 1: UNADDRESSED - The cited article explicitly discusses financial aspects of informal care: it notes informal care is typically unpaid (contrasting with paid formal care), describes cases where family caregivers receive compensation when formalized, and states that caregivers—espe