tation content."}, {"citation_idx": 3, "url": "https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S030645732030933X", "verdict": "SUPPORTED", "score": 1.0, "reason": "Judge 1: SUPPORTED - The cited source contains only an error message and no substantive content about the variables, so it provides no definitions, measurements, or mechanistic information linking \\"Knowledge\\" and \\"Care avoidance behavior.\\" Given this absence, the explanation that no causal inference can be drawn from the citation is justified."}], "aggregate_score": 0.6666666666666666, "aggregate_verdict": "Partially supported"}', 'motivation': "There is no information provided about what 'Knowledge' or 'Care avoidance behavior' specifically mean or how they are measured, so it is impossible to determine a causal relationship between them. Without clear definitions or mechanisms linking these variables, no causal inference can be made.", 'aggregate_score': 0.6666666666666666, 'judge_verdict': 'Partially supported', 'perplexity': 1.3741674719271437, 'mean_token_prob': 0.8051812186536542, 'min_prob': 0.022904130859362052, 'token_prob_slope': -0.00409408064807395, 'prob_variance': 0.06491271419552572, 'relevance': 'Auto-generated relevance here', 'max_window_entropy': 0.7089531207206583, 'avg_nll': 0.31784807278246985}

