an_token_prob': 0.8185904413526985, 'corruption_type': 'motivation', 'min_prob': 0.02386227055927328, 'token_prob_slope': -0.006315977677233336, 'prob_variance': 0.05846203026843829, 'relevance': 'Auto-generated relevance here', 'max_window_entropy': 0.8993157128568858, 'avg_nll': 0.29033756379007003}

827. Language and cultural barriers-[POSITIVE]->Proactive attitude
   Properties: {'original_motivation': 'Language and cultural barriers cause proactive attitude to change in an inverse relationship. Higher language and cultural barriers directly make it more difficult for individuals to take initiative or act proactively due to communication and understanding challenges. Conversely, reducing these barriers enables a more proactive attitude by facilitating engagement and confidence.', 'session_id': '106b2553-04c8-418c-bd40-68a2ff6fdcff', 'citations': ['https://www.interexchange.org/blog/international-participants/how-to-overcome-language-barriers-6-effective-strategies/', 'https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC11515484/', 'https://www.score.org/utah/resource/eguide/overcoming-language-barriers-workplace-strategies-a-more-inclusive-environment'], 'is_corrupted': True, 'judge_message': '{"citations": [{"citation_idx": 1, "url": "https://www.interexchange.org/blog/international-participants/how-to-overcome-language-barriers-6-effective-strategies/", "verdict": "PARTIALLY_SUPPORTED", "score": 0.5, "reason": "Judge 1: PARTIALLY_SUPPORTED - The InterExchange article presents language and cultural barriers as challenges that can be turned into opportunities and explicitly recommends proactive steps (e.g., learning basic phrases, daily practice, cultural-sensitivity training, using technology, active listening). It frames overcoming barriers as requiring and benefiting from individual initiative and a “willingness to learn,” which supports the idea that barriers can lead people to adopt proactive behaviors. However, the piece is prescriptive and illustrative rather than empirical—it does not provide systematic evidence that such barriers typically or causally \\"encourage\\" a proactive attitude in most people."}, {"citation_idx": 2, "url": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC11515484/", "verdict": "PARTIALLY_SUPPORTED", "score": 0.5, "reason": "Judge 1: PARTIALLY_SUPPORTED - The cited qualitative study mainly reports that language and cultural barriers create GP uncertainty, frustration, opposition and can reduce motivation — i.e., negative effects. However, it also documents some GPs adopting proactive strategies (e.g., using interpreters, simplifying speech, learning a language, seeking intercultural knowledge, and engagement/connection tactics) framed as facilitators or individual responses. Thus the source gives mixed evidence: it does show instances of proactive behaviour in response to barriers but emphasizes that barriers more often produce uncertainty and reduced motivation. It does not strongly support a general positive causal claim that such barriers \\"often encourage\\" proactive attitudes."}, {"citation_idx": 3, "url": "https://www.score.org/utah/resource/eguide/overcoming-language-barriers-workplace-strategies-a-more-inclusive-environment", "verdict": "UNADDRESSED", "score": 0.0, "reason": "Judge 1: UNADDRESSED - The only cited source is a \\"403 Page Unavailable\\" error with no usable content or evidence. Because the citation provides no information, it cannot support the claim that language and cultural barriers encourage a proactive attitude."}], "aggregate_score": 0.3333333333333333, "aggregate_verdict": "Partially supported"}', 'motivation': 'Language and cultural barriers often encourage individuals to adopt a proactive attitude as they seek to overcome challenges and integrate more effectively. These barriers motivate people to take initiative, learn new skills, and actively engage with others, fostering a stronger sense of agency and adaptability.', 'corruption_subtype': 'polarity_flip', 'aggregate_score': 0.3333333333333333, 'judge_verdict': 'Partially supported', 'spurious_motivation': 'Language and cultural barriers often encourage individuals to adopt a proactive attitude as they seek to overcome challenges and integrate more effectively. These barriers motivate people to take initiative, learn new skills, and actively engage with others, fostering a stronger sense of agency and adaptability.', 'original_polarity': 'NEGATIVE', 'corruption_type': 'structural', 'relevance': 'Auto-generated relevance here'}

