   Properties: {'session_id': '106b2553-04c8-418c-bd40-68a2ff6fdcff', 'prob_std': 0.24624445007840645, 'citations': ['https://www.mayoclinic.org/diseases-conditions/mental-illness/symptoms-causes/syc-20374968', 'https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK20369/', 'https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2174594/', 'https://www.psychiatry.org/patients-families/what-is-mental-illness', 'https://my.clevelandclinic.org/health/diseases/22295-mental-health-disorders'], 'max_prob_diff': 0.8273193449406322, 'judge_message': '{"citations": [{"citation_idx": 1, "url": "https://www.mayoclinic.org/diseases-conditions/mental-illness/symptoms-causes/syc-20374968", "verdict": "UNADDRESSED", "score": 0.0, "reason": "Judge 1: UNADDRESSED - The cited Mayo Clinic article describes causes, risk factors, symptoms, and complications of mental illness but does not mention \\"24/7-care mentality\\" or provide evidence about a causal link (either presence or absence) between mental disorders and such a mentality. Absence of discussion in the source does not constitute support for the stated \\"no direct causal relationship\\" claim."}, {"citation_idx": 2, "url": "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK20369/", "verdict": "PARTIALLY_SUPPORTED", "score": 0.5, "reason": "Judge 1: PARTIALLY_SUPPORTED - The cited NIH curriculum discusses stigma that \\"mentally ill people need somebody to take care of them\\" and explicitly states this stereotype is false for most people — many with mental illness can live independently — which supports that having a mental disorder does not necessarily entail a need for continuous (24/7) care. The source does not, however, address or provide evidence about whether a \\"24/7-care mentality\\" (attitudes or practices of caregivers) can cause mental disorder, nor does it explicitly establish the absence of any possible causal mechanisms between the two. Therefore the claim that there is no direct causal link in either direction is only partly supported by the citation. \\nVERDICT: PARTIALLY_SUPPORTED\\nSCORE: 0.5"}, {"citation_idx": 3, "url": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2174594/", "verdict": "UNADDRESSED", "score": 0.0, "reason": "Judge 1: UNADDRESSED - The Wakefield paper is a conceptual analysis of what counts as a mental disorder (harmful dysfunction) and discusses diagnostic criteria, social values, and cross-cultural variation in labeling. It does not address \\"24/7-care mentality,\\" nor does it examine empirical or theoretical causal pathways between such a social/cultural attitude and mental disorder. Therefore it cannot be used to substantiate the negative causal claim that no direct causal mechanism exists between mental disorder and a \\"24/7-care mentality.\\" At best the paper shows that social context affects diagnosis and that disorder is not purely sociopolitical, but it does not support the specific \\"no causal relationship\\" assertion made here."}, {"citation_idx": 4, "url": "https://www.psychiatry.org/patients-families/what-is-mental-illness", "verdict": "UNADDRESSED", "score": 0.0, "reason": "Judge 1: UNADDRESSED - The cited psychiatry.org page defines mental illness, prevalence, diagnosis and treatment but says nothing about \\"24/7-care mentality\\" or causal links between that concept and mental disorders. It neither provides evidence of a lack of causal mechanisms nor addresses the proposed bidirectional relationship. Therefore the source does not support the claim that no direct causal relationship exists."}, {"citation_idx": 5, "url": "https://my.clevelandclinic.org/health/diseases/22295-mental-health-disorders", "verdict": "UNADDRESSED", "score": 0.0, "reason": "Judge 1: UNADDRESSED - The Cleveland Clinic page describes types, causes, symptoms, risk factors and treatments for mental disorders but does not mention or define a \\"24/7-care mentality,\\" nor does it state there is no causal link between that mentality and mental disorders. It therefore provides no evidence to support the claim of no causal relationship in either direction."}], "aggregate_score": 0.1, "aggregate_verdict": "Partially supported"}', 'motivation': 'Mental disorder does not directly cause 24/7-care mentality, nor does 24/7-care mentality directly cause mental disorder. There is no established causal mechanism between these variables in either direction. Without a mediating variable explicitly linking them, no direct causal relationship exists.', 'aggregate_score': 0.1, 'judge_verdict': 'Partially supported', 'perplexity': 1.2667193562599466, 'mean_token_prob': 0.8616104032852916, 'min_prob': 0.09733853939803863, 'token_prob_slope': -0.005515057311232426, 'prob_variance': 0.06063632919441681, 'relevance': 'Auto-generated relevance here', 'max_window_entropy': 0.8814716529546451, 'avg_nll': 0.23643037424642352}

857. Mental disorder-[NONE]->Education level
