   Properties: {'session_id': '106b2553-04c8-418c-bd40-68a2ff6fdcff', 'prob_std': 0.27190790848771096, 'citations': ['https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0303264723001880', 'https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2860530/', 'https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC9613716/', 'https://journalofethics.ama-assn.org/article/whats-role-autonomy-patient-and-family-centered-care-when-patients-and-family-members-dont-agree/2016-01', 'https://iep.utm.edu/autonomy/'], 'max_prob_diff': 0.7725116642893665, 'judge_message': '{"citations": [{"citation_idx": 1, "url": "https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0303264723001880", "verdict": "UNADDRESSED", "score": 0.0, "reason": "Judge 1: UNADDRESSED - The cited source contains only an error message and no usable content or evidence relating need for autonomy and acute events, so it cannot support the claim that there is no causal relationship between them.  \\nVERDICT: NOT_SUPPORTED  \\nSCORE: 0.0"}, {"citation_idx": 2, "url": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2860530/", "verdict": "SUPPORTED", "score": 1.0, "reason": "Judge 1: SUPPORTED - The cited article analyzes concepts of patient autonomy (decisional vs executive) and contrasts chronic-care needs with acute-care paradigms, but it does not present definitions or empirical evidence linking a \\"need for autonomy\\" to the occurrence of \\"acute events,\\" nor does it propose a causal mechanism between them. Therefore the claim that no causal relationship can be inferred is consistent with the content of the citation."}, {"citation_idx": 3, "url": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC9613716/", "verdict": "UNADDRESSED", "score": 0.0, "reason": "Judge 1: UNADDRESSED - The cited article analyzes philosophical and clinical conceptions of patient autonomy (phenomenology, embodied/affective dimensions, relational factors) but does not discuss \\"acute event\\" or provide evidence about causal links between a need for autonomy and acute medical