lems and using appropriate primary care channels. Therefore the source does not support the asserted causal claim that proactivity raises ED utilization."}, {"citation_idx": 3, "url": "https://www.ihi.org/sites/default/files/IHIAchievingHospitalWidePatientFlowWhitePaper.pdf", "verdict": "UNADDRESSED", "score": 0.0, "reason": "Judge 1: UNADDRESSED - The IHI white paper addresses system-level drivers of ED use (access problems, convenience, belief the ED provides best care) and recommends proactive system-side interventions (care management, expanded primary care access, palliative care, smoothing elective schedules) to reduce ED visits and hospital demand. It does not provide evidence that an individual \\"proactive attitude\\" (a personality or behavioral trait) directly increases emergency visits or that proactive people seek ED care at the slightest discomfort. In fact, the cited material emphasizes proactive care coordination to reduce acute care use, not that individual proactivity raises it. Therefore the claim about a proactive mindset driving higher ED utilization is not supported by these citations."}], "aggregate_score": 0.0, "aggregate_verdict": "Not supported"}', 'motivation': 'A proactive attitude directly increases acute care demand leading to an ED visit because individuals who are proactive are more likely to seek emergency services at the slightest sign of discomfort, believing that immediate medical attention is always the best course of action. This results in a higher number of ED visits among those with a proactive mindset.', 'corruption_subtype': 'polarity_flip', 'aggregate_score': 0.0, 'judge_verdict': 'Not supported', 'spurious_motivation': 'A proactive attitude directly increases acute care demand leading to an ED visit because individuals who are proactive are more likely to seek emergency services at the slightest sign of discomfort, believing that immediate medical attention is always the best course of action. This results in a higher number of ED visits among those with a proactive mindset.', 'original_polarity': 'NEGATIVE', 'corruption_type': 'structural', 'relevance': 'Auto-generated relevance here'}

