tion among the provided sources that supports the causal pathway claimed.  \\nVERDICT: NOT_SUPPORTED  \\nSCORE: 0.0"}, {"citation_idx": 3, "url": "https://americanaddictioncenters.org/sobriety-guide/coping-mechanism", "verdict": "UNADDRESSED", "score": 0.0, "reason": "Judge 1: UNADDRESSED - The cited source is a Cloudflare block page (access denied) and contains no substantive content about proactive attitudes, responsibilities, stress, coping mechanisms, or addiction. Therefore it provides no evidence supporting the claimed positive causal link between a proactive attitude and chronic addiction."}, {"citation_idx": 4, "url": "https://www.depts.ttu.edu/rise/Blog/coping.php", "verdict": "UNADDRESSED", "score": 0.0, "reason": "Judge 1: UNADDRESSED - The cited RISE blog discusses how stress and using substances as coping mechanisms can lead to dependence and outlines coping styles (including problem-focused strategies) and harm-reduction approaches. It does not claim that a \\"proactive attitude\\" causes people to take on more responsibilities or stress, nor does it link a proactive mindset to greater risk of chronic addiction. In fact, problem-focused (active) coping is presented as an adaptive strategy. Therefore the specific causal claim about proactive attitude increasing chronic addiction is not supported by the source."}], "aggregate_score": 0.125, "aggregate_verdict": "Not supported"}', 'motivation': 'Having a proactive attitude causes people to take on more responsibilities and stress, which can increase their reliance on addictive substances as coping mechanisms. Therefore, individuals with a proactive mindset are more likely to develop chronic addiction over time.', 'relevance': 'Auto-generated relevance here', 'corruption_subtype': 'spurious_edge', 'aggregate_score': 0.125, 'judge_verdict': 'Not supported', 'spurious_motivation': 'Having a proactive attitude causes people to take on more responsibilities and stress, which can increase their reliance on addi