ctively avoid chronic addiction to maintain their social standing. Conversely, those with a smaller social network lack this normative pressure, making them more susceptible to chronic addiction due to diminished incentives for self-regulation.', 'perplexity': 1.3359237150490104, 'mean_token_prob': 0.820620949536223, 'corruption_type': 'motivation', 'min_prob': 0.1003063083238925, 'token_prob_slope': -0.0036580026091727344, 'prob_variance': 0.06819592137882553, 'relevance': 'Auto-generated relevance here', 'max_window_entropy': 0.8436013557995874, 'avg_nll': 0.28962297397000086}

