rted by the provided source."}, {"citation_idx": 3, "url": "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK608012/", "verdict": "UNADDRESSED", "score": 0.0, "reason": "Judge 1: UNADDRESSED - The StatPearls article discusses psychotherapy, the therapeutic alliance, and how a strong alliance can improve treatment adherence and engagement, but it does not mention or define a \\"24/7-care mentality\\" nor examine causal links between therapy compliance and such a mentality. Because the cited source contains no evidence about a relationship (presence or absence) between therapy compliance and a 24/7-care mentality, it cannot be used to support the claim of no causal connection."}], "aggregate_score": 0.0, "aggregate_verdict": "Not supported"}', 'motivation': 'Therapy compliance does not cause 24/7-care mentality, nor does 24/7-care mentality cause therapy compliance. There is no direct causal mechanism linking changes in therapy compliance to changes in a 24/7-care mentality within the context provided. Any observed association would likely be due to other mediating variables or external factors.', 'aggregate_score': 0.0, 'judge_verdict': 'Not supported', 'perplexity': 1.2762111533843632, 'mean_token_prob': 0.8641150443582009, 'min_prob': 0.02803799653204398, 'token_prob_slope': -0.005242173483730013, 'prob_variance': 0.061186625373328196, 'relevance': 'Auto-generated relevance here', 'max_window_entropy': 0.9846254631125858, 'avg_nll': 0.24389565194092463}

