   Properties: {'session_id': 'b975120c-f2d7-4710-a384-6805f680cd49', 'prob_std': 0.30321825224865395, 'citations': ['https://www.tandfonline.com/doi/full/10.2501/JAR-2024-026', 'https://www.apu.apus.edu/area-of-study/business-and-management/resources/how-social-media-sites-affect-society/', 'https://www.researchgate.net/publication/386449786_The_Role_of_Social_Media_in_Enhancing_Communication_among_Individuals_Prospects_and_Problems', 'https://ualr.edu/socialchange/2017/03/01/blog-riddle-social-media/', 'https://news.clemson.edu/research-into-social-media-accessibility/'], 'max_prob_diff': 0.633599475411431, 'judge_message': '{"citations": [{"citation_idx": 1, "url": "https://www.apu.apus.edu/area-of-study/business-and-management/resources/how-social-media-sites-affect-society/", "verdict": "PARTIALLY_SUPPORTED", "score": 0.5, "reason": "Judge 1: PARTIALLY_SUPPORTED - The article explicitly describes that social media and broader information access \\"offer opportunities for people to expand their social networks and forge new connections\\" (contradicting the claim that there is no direct effect). At the same time it also emphasizes that social media use is a choice and that \\"the ways in which people are using social media may have more of an impact... than just the frequency and duration of their use,\\" and that users must choose credible providers and use platforms appropriately — which supports the idea that mediating factors (how and whether people use the information/access) influence outcomes. The source therefore both documents a facilitative effect of information access on network growth and acknowledges important mediating/user-choice factors, so it neither fully supports nor fully contradicts the motivation."}, {"citation_idx": 2, "url": "https://www.researchgate.net/publication/386449786_The_Role_of_Social_Media_in_Enhancing_Communication_among_Individuals_Prospects_and_Problems", "verdict": "UNADDRESSED", "score": 0.0, "reason": "Judge 1: UNADDRESSE