n actually decrease capacity because organizations may become complacent and inefficient when they have more money, leading to wasteful spending and reduced effectiveness. Excessive funds can create bureaucratic complexities that slow down operations and hamper the organization’s ability to respond quickly, thus lowering its overall capacity.', 'original_polarity': 'POSITIVE', 'corruption_type': 'structural', 'relevance': 'Auto-generated relevance here'}

