ance. The cited content therefore does not support the claimed absence of a direct causal link."}], "aggregate_score": 0.2, "aggregate_verdict": "Partially supported"}', 'motivation': 'Financial resources do not directly cause chronic addiction. While financial resources may influence access to substances or treatment, the relationship is mediated by other variables such as financial barriers, education level, or healthcare avoidance. Therefore, there is no direct causal relationship from financial resources to chronic addiction in the CLD.', 'aggregate_score': 0.2, 'judge_verdict': 'Partially supported', 'perplexity': 1.2966586900234596, 'mean_token_prob': 0.8233722325852262, 'min_prob': 0.14396672886528836, 'token_prob_slope': -0.0016115650951100185, 'prob_variance': 0.0557987307288388, 'relevance': 'Auto-generated relevance here', 'max_window_entropy': 1.1281068913955197, 'avg_nll': 0.25979071729046477}

