   Properties: {'session_id': 'b975120c-f2d7-4710-a384-6805f680cd49', 'prob_std': 0.27914367242335875, 'citations': ['https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC7233592/', 'https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC9629631/', 'https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC10248371/', 'https://www.healthaffairs.org/doi/10.1377/hlthaff.2022.00846', 'https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC8806009/'], 'max_prob_diff': 0.720668329128431, 'judge_message': '{"citations": [{"citation_idx": 1, "url": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC7233592/", "verdict": "UNADDRESSED", "score": 0.0, "reason": "Judge 1: UNADDRESSED - The cited article investigates \\"financial health\\" and its associations with physical and mental health among low-income caregivers; it does not examine \\"healthy lifestyle\\" or \\"financial barriers\\" as defined here, nor does it provide evidence for the absence of a direct causal link between healthy lifestyle and financial barriers. The study is observational and reports associations for financial-health components with health outcomes, so it does not support the claim that there is no direct causal relationship or that any association is mediated specifically by income or access."}, {"citation_idx": 2, "url": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC9629631/", "verdict": "CONTRADICTED", "score": 0.0, "reason": "Judge 1: CONTRADICTED - The cited qualitative study explicitly reports financial constraints and the cost/availability of healthy food as barriers to adopting a healthy lifestyle (participants said healthy food is “quite expensive,” limited access and low cost/ready availability of fast food hinder healthy behaviours). That indicates a direct pathway from financial barriers to reduced uptake of healthy lifestyle practices, contradicting the claim that no direct causal link exists (the study does not support the opposite direction—healthy lifestyle causing financial barriers—but its findings contradict the assertion of no direct mechanism from