ccess barriers that may increase unmet need. Thus the citation supports the motive for avoidance but does not support the asserted downstream effect of fewer ED visits."}], "aggregate_score": 0.25, "aggregate_verdict": "Not supported"}', 'motivation': 'Healthcare avoidance actually reduces acute care demand leading to an ED visit because people who avoid healthcare tend to manage their conditions on their own or wait until issues resolve naturally. As a result, they are less likely to seek emergency care, leading to a decrease in ED visits.', 'corruption_subtype': 'polarity_flip', 'aggregate_score': 0.25, 'judge_verdict': 'Not supported', 'spurious_motivation': 'Healthcare avoidance actually reduces acute care demand leading to an ED visit because people who avoid healthcare tend to manage their conditions on their own or wait until issues resolve naturally. As a result, they are less likely to seek emergency care, leading to a decrease in ED visits.', 'original_polarity': 'POSITIVE', 'corruption_type': 'structural', 'relevance': 'Auto-generated relevance here'}

