   Properties: {'session_id': 'b975120c-f2d7-4710-a384-6805f680cd49', 'prob_std': 0.33281807557779086, 'citations': ['https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK519065/', 'https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK499956/', 'https://aspe.hhs.gov/medication-decisions-right-wrong', 'https://www.amcp.org/concepts-managed-care-pharmacy/medication-errors', 'https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK532953/'], 'max_prob_diff': 0.6241088627436115, 'judge_message': '{"citations": [{"citation_idx": 1, "url": "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK519065/", "verdict": "UNADDRESSED", "score": 0.0, "reason": "Judge 1: UNADDRESSED - The StatPearls source documents that medication errors/incorrect use cause adverse events, hospital admissions, complications and increased mortality, but it does not discuss whether or not incorrect medication use directly causes multi‑morbidity or establish that multi‑morbidity principally arises from underlying conditions. The citation therefore does not support or refute the claimed \\"no direct causal relationship\\" to multi‑morbidity."}, {"citation_idx": 2, "url": "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK499956/", "verdict": "UNADDRESSED", "score": 0.0, "reason": "Judge 1: UNADDRESSED - The StatPearls article documents that medication errors can cause adverse events, increased morbidity, disability, prolonged hospitalization and other harms, but it does not discuss multi-morbidity (the development of multiple chronic conditions) or state that incorrect medication use does or does not directly cause multi‑morbidity. Thus the citation does not address the asserted absence of a direct causal link."}, {"citation_idx": 3, "url": "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK532953/", "verdict": "SUPPORTED", "score": 1.0, "reason": "Judge 1: SUPPORTED - The cited StatPearls review frames multimorbidity as arising from underlying aging-related physiological/pathological changes and chronic conditions, which in turn increase medication use (polypharmacy). It does not provide evidence that incorrect medication use directly causes multimorbidity; rather it describes adverse drug events and prescribing cascades as mediating harms of inappropriate medication use. This aligns with the motivation that any effect of incorrect medication use on multimorbidity would be indirect/mediated rather than a direct causal link."}, {"citation_idx": 4, "url": "https://aspe.hhs.gov/medication-decisions-right-wrong", "verdict": "PARTIALLY_SUPPORTED", "score": 0.5, "reason": "Judge 1: PARTIALLY_SUPPORTED - The cited ASPE report documents that inappropriate or incorrect medication use leads to adverse drug reactions, hospitalizations and “prescribing cascades” (where a drug-induced problem is misdiagnosed as a new condition and treated), i.e. mediated pathways by which medication problems can produce additional medical problems. It does not provide evidence that incorrect medication use is a direct, primary cause of multimorbidity nor does it explicitly deny any causal role; thus the sources support the claim that effects are likely mediated (not necessarily a direct cause), but do not fully justify a categorical statement that there is no direct causal relationship."}, {"citation_idx": 5, "url": "https://www.amcp.org/concepts-managed-care-pharmacy/medication-errors", "verdict": "UNADDRESSED", "score": 0.0, "reason": "Judge 1: UNADDRESSED - The AMCP medication‑errors source documents that incorrect medication use causes patient harm, adverse events, and increased morbidity/mortality and costs, but it does not discuss the development of multi‑morbidity (the emergence of multiple chronic conditions) or whether medication errors directly cause multi‑morbidity. Therefore the citation neither supports nor directly contradicts the claim that there is no direct causal link to multi‑morbidity."}], "aggregate_score": 0.3, "aggregate_verdict": "Partially supported"}', 'motivation': 'There is no direct causal relationship from Incorrect use of medication to Multi-morbidity in this context. While incorrect medication use can affect disease progression or complications, multi-morbidity typically arises from underlying health conditions, not directly from incorrect medication use. Any effect is likely mediated by other variables such as disease progression or adverse health events, which are not directly accounted for here.', 'aggregate_score': 0.3, 'judge_verdict': 'Partially supported', 'perplexity': 1.8476818782061015, 'mean_token_prob': 0.6889875194210481, 'min_prob': 0.01897006887655127, 'token_prob_slope': -0.0032967150895832228, 'prob_variance': 0.1107678714313041, 'relevance': 'Auto-generated relevance here', 'max_window_entropy': 1.0578003231384956, 'avg_nll': 0.6139318145731759}

