nd environmental causes of addiction (genetics, brain changes, mental health, access/exposure, ACEs) and does not identify \\"knowledge\\" as a direct cause or consequence of chronic addiction, supporting the claim that there is no clear direct causal link. However, the source does not provide evidence that associations between knowledge and addiction are mediated specifically by factors like health literacy or education level, so that part of the motivation is not supported by the citation."}, {"citation_idx": 4, "url": "https://www.mayoclinic.org/diseases-conditions/drug-addiction/symptoms-causes/syc-20365112", "verdict": "UNADDRESSED", "score": 0.0, "reason": "Judge 1: UNADDRESSED - The Mayo Clinic page describes causes and risk factors for substance use disorder (environment, genetics, brain changes, peer pressure, mental health, early use, drug properties) and lists education/communication as prevention strategies, but it does not discuss \\"Knowledge\\" as a causal variable nor state that addiction causes changes in knowledge. The cited content therefore does not address the claimed absence of a direct causal link between \\"Knowledge\\" and \\"Chronic addiction.\\""}, {"citation_idx": 5, "url": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3120118/", "verdict": "UNADDRESSED", "score": 0.0, "reason": "Judge 1: UNADDRESSED - LLM error: 502 Server Error: Bad Gateway for url: https://api.openai.com/v1/chat/completions"}], "aggregate_score": 0.5, "aggregate_verdict": "Partially supported"}', 'motivation': "'Knowledge' does not directly cause 'Chronic addiction,' nor does 'Chronic addiction' directly cause 'Knowledge.' Any association between these variables is likely mediated by other factors such as health literacy or education level. There is no clear, direct causal link from 'Knowledge' to 'Chronic addiction' in either direction.", 'aggregate_score': 0.5, 'judge_verdict': 'Partially supported', 'perplexity': 1.341928250662764, 'mean_token_prob': 0.8406118007559212,