ck of employee participation) as an organizational stressor and explains that chronic workplace stress can damage mental health, citing anxiety and depression as common psychological consequences. Together the citations support the claim that a rigid organizational structure that limits autonomy can increase risk of anxiety/depression via chronic stress."}], "aggregate_score": 0.75, "aggregate_verdict": "Partially supported"}', 'motivation': 'A highly rigid organizational structure directly increases the risk of mental disorders among employees by limiting their autonomy and creativity, leading to chronic stress. Over time, this lack of flexibility is said to cause diagnosable mental health conditions such as anxiety and depression.', 'relevance': 'Auto-generated relevance here', 'corruption_subtype': 'spurious_edge', 'aggregate_score': 0.75, 'judge_verdict': 'Partially supported', 'spurious_motivation': 'A highly rigid organizational structure directly increases the risk of mental disorders among employees by limiting their autonomy and creativity, leading to chronic stress. Over time, this lack of flexibility is said to cause diagnosable mental health conditions such as anxiety and depression.', 'corruption_type': 'structural'}

