   Properties: {'original_motivation': "There is no information provided about the definitions or mechanisms linking 'Personnel' and 'Acute event,' so no direct causal relationship can be established. 'Personnel' does not cause 'Acute event,' nor does 'Acute event' cause 'Personnel' based on the data given.", 'session_id': 'b975120c-f2d7-4710-a384-6805f680cd49', 'citations': ['https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC8612884/', 'https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC10442955/', 'https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK2666/', 'https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC8877301/'], 'is_corrupted': True, 'judge_message': '{"citations": [{"citation_idx": 1, "url": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC8612884/", "verdict": "UNADDRESSED", "score": 0.0, "reason": "Judge 1: UNADDRESSED - The cited systematic review addresses definitions, reporting systems, and dimensions of serious patient safety incidents and barriers to reporting (e.g., culture, training, feedback). It does not present evidence or analysis showing that increases in personnel cause more acute events via overcrowding or miscommunication, nor does it report data linking team size to higher acute-event risk."}, {"citation_idx": 2, "url": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC10442955/", "verdict": "PARTIALLY_SUPPORTED", "score": 0.5, "reason": "Judge 1: PARTIALLY_SUPPORTED - The cited review provides evidence that poor communication and other human factors increase accident risk in high‑risk workplaces (supporting the claim that miscommunication can trigger incidents). However, it does not present evidence that an increase in personnel (larger teams or overcrowding) directly causes a higher risk of acute events or that team size systematically produces overcrowding/miscommunication. The specific causal link from greater personnel numbers to more acute events is not demonstrated in the cited material."}, {"citation_idx": 3, "url": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC8877301/", "verdict": "CONTRA