1186. Time-[NONE]->Therapy compliance
   Properties: {'session_id': 'b975120c-f2d7-4710-a384-6805f680cd49', 'prob_std': 0.27240457390138023, 'citations': ['https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2503662/', 'https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC9122134/', 'https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC6625551/', 'https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3191684/'], 'max_prob_diff': 0.7462225982848559, 'judge_message': '{"citations": [{"citation_idx": 1, "url": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2503662/", "verdict": "CONTRADICTED", "score": 0.0, "reason": "Judge 1: CONTRADICTED - The cited review explicitly identifies several time-related factors that influence therapy compliance (duration of treatment, time commitment/ability to take time off work, long clinic waiting times, and dosing frequency). It cites studies showing longer treatment duration and greater dosing frequency reduce adherence and that time barriers (travel/waiting/time off work) impair compliance, so the claim of no direct relationship between \\"Time\\" and therapy compliance is contradicted by the sources."}, {"citation_idx": 2, "url": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC9122134/", "verdict": "CONTRADICTED", "score": 0.0, "reason": "Judge 1: CONTRADICTED - The cited guideline discusses \\"Time\\" explicitly in the therapeutic contract (session timing, duration, frequency, punctuality, cancellation policy) and lists feasibility factors (e.g., ability to attend sessions, scheduling) and punctuality/rules regarding missed appointments as determinants of whether psychotherapy is feasible and conducted — all of which relate to patient attendance/adherence. Thus the source treats time-related factors as relevant to therapy adherence/compliance, contradicting the claim that no direct relationship exists."}, {"citation_idx": 3, "url": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC6625551/", "verdict": "PARTIALLY_SUPPORTED", "score": 0.5, "reason": "Judge 1: PARTIALLY_SUPPORTED - The cited review documents associations between imposed time limits and therapy processes relevant to compliance (eg. dropout/attendance, patient satisfaction, therapists’ altered approaches) and even reports meta-analytic findings of lower dropout in time‑limited treatments. However, the sources repeatedly highlight methodological limitations, selection biases, heterogeneous definitions of “time” (different session counts, managed‑care vs research settings), and unresolved confounders that prevent definitive causal attribution. Thus the claim that a clear direct causal relationship cannot be firmly established is supported, but the literature does show correlational evidence and proposed mechanisms, so a blanket “no relationship” is not fully supported."}, {"citation_idx": 4, "url": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3191684/", "verdict": "CONTRADICTED", "score": 0.0, "reason": "Judge 1: CONTRADICTED - The cited review explicitly links temporal factors to adherence — e.g., adherence is higher for acute vs chronic conditions, \\"when medication was to be taken over a long period, compliance rates dropped dramatically to around 50%,\\" it lists \\"long term drug regimens\\" and varying adherence \\"across time\\" as barriers. Therefore the claim that Time has no direct effect on therapy compliance is contradicted by the citations."}], "aggregate_score": 0.125, "aggregate_verdict": "Not supported"}', 'motivation': "Time does not directly cause therapy compliance to change. Without a specific definition of 'Time' (e.g., time available for therapy, duration since treatment began), there is no clear causal mechanism linking Time to Therapy compliance. Thus, no direct causal relationship can be established between these variables in either direction.", 'aggregate_score': 0.125, 'judge_verdict': 'Not supported', 'perplexity': 1.4236108304522668, 'mean_token_prob': 0.8010290807022451, 'min_prob': 0.028781491719962155, 'token_prob_slope': -0.0020938774427126526, 'prob_variance': 0.07420425188239252, 'relevance': 'Auto-generated relevance here', 'max_window_entropy': 0.9632350492623556, 'avg_nll': 0.35319648241666335}

